WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.740
A loaf of bread.

2
00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:02.960
A lamp.

3
00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:04.530
A shepherd's crook.

4
00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:05.900
A vine.

5
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:10.720
In John's Gospel, Jesus
says: I am the bread of life.

6
00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:13.060
I am the light of the world.

7
00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.150
I am the good shepherd.

8
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.470
I am the true vine.

9
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.660
None of these sayings appears in Matthew,

10
00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.160
Mark or Luke.

11
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:25.680
So why does Jesus in John describe
himself with everyday things?

12
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:29.230
In this mission, you'll take
the four sayings one at a time,

13
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.290
with the festival or
moment each belongs to.

14
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.650
Then you'll weigh up a sharper question:
are these sayings claims to be God?

15
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:41.790
Your mission: find out why
John's Jesus chooses bread,

16
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.200
light, a shepherd and a vine.
